    fix(api): expose version in /health response for SPA chip. Addresses REVIEW-OB-021.
    
    The SPA status chip (web/js/app.js) reads j.version from /health, but the
    endpoint only returned status+uptime, so web/index.html shipped the static
    "v0.0.0" fallback forever. Add Server.Version, set it from main's
    ldflags-injected version variable after construction (same idiom as
    ExportLocalDir/Observer; keeps api.New signature stable for the muster
    e2e_test.go caller), and emit it in the handleHealth JSON map.
    
    New test TestHealthReportsVersion (server_test.go) pins the contract:
    known version string round-trips, status stays "ok", uptime present.
    
    Verified: go build ./... OK, go vet ./... OK, full suite
    ./... -count=1 -short -parallel 4 green (16 pkgs), and a scratch binary
    stamped -X main.version=0.2.1-review021 serves
    {"status":"ok","uptime":"4s","version":"0.2.1-review021"} on /health.
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
